# Grid A — S1 Explain / Mechanism drill-down (runTaskGraph failure path)
#
# Targets: architecture_explain + ReqCallChain + ShapeStepList.
# Validate node failure has a fine-grained backtrack that requeues
# only upstream evidence nodes (not the whole graph), using
# EdgeValidationFeedback guards. Answer must name the specific
# functions involved so we can verify it reached the right code.
#
# Ground truth (internal/orchestrator/scheduler.go): a failed validate
# node calls markSuccessCriteriaFailed on the node, and uses
# EdgeValidationFeedback edges to requeue upstream evidence nodes.
# Negative anchors block the "whole graph restarts" hallucination
# and the deleted write-pipeline roles (CodeReviewer / Planner /
# DesignReviewer) that the LLM sometimes invents from training data.
ID="s1b"
NAME="mechanism drill-down — runTaskGraph validate failure fine-grained backtrack"
QUESTION="How does runTaskGraph's criterion-aware window scheduler handle a failed validate node — which upstream nodes get requeued, and does the whole DAG restart?"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: EC has 3 specific function names
# (good) + ENC blocks wrong roles. Add EMR to gate the binary
# question "whole DAG restart" — answer must explicitly say no/不
# (selective requeue, not whole restart). Generic listing of 3
# function names without addressing the binary axis no longer
# PASSes.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="runTaskGraph EdgeValidationFeedback markSuccessCriteriaFailed"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(\bno\b|not.*restart|partial|selective|不会.*重启|仅.*重排|不重启)
(upstream|前置|evidence node|证据)"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="CodeReviewer Planner DesignReviewer .java"
